I have a complete picture. The MCP surface delegates to the same gRPC `MemoService_ListMemos`/`GetMemo` operations (see `server/router/mcp/catalog.go`), so it reuses the API v1 enforcement rather than having its own. Here is the full inventory of distinct server-side visibility-enforcement sites.

## Core API v1 (gRPC/Connect) — the canonical single-memo gate

**`server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go`** — `checkMemoReadAccess` (lines 39-68). This is the central read-access helper used by GetMemo and ListMemoComments.
```go
if memo.RowStatus == store.Archived { ... memo.CreatorID != user.ID -> NotFound }
if memo.Visibility != store.Public {
    if user == nil { return Unauthenticated }
    if memo.Visibility == store.Private && memo.CreatorID != user.ID {
        return PermissionDenied
    }
}
```
Callers: `GetMemo` (lines 356 and 367 — also re-checks the parent memo for comments), and `ListMemoComments` in `memo_service_comments.go:148`.

**`server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go`** — `ListMemos` (lines 178-227). List enforcement is done by building store filters, not per-row checks:
```go
if currentUser == nil {
    memoFind.VisibilityList = []store.Visibility{store.Public}
} else {
    if memoFind.CreatorID == nil {
        filter := fmt.Sprintf(`creator_id == %d || visibility in ["PUBLIC", "PROTECTED"]`, currentUser.ID)
        memoFind.Filters = append(memoFind.Filters, filter)
    } else if *memoFind.CreatorID != currentUser.ID {
        memoFind.VisibilityList = []store.Visibility{store.Public, store.Protected}
    }
}
```
Archived state (lines 188-199) additionally pins `CreatorID` to the current user.

## Store layer — where VisibilityList becomes SQL

**`store/db/sqlite/memo.go`** (lines 96-103), **`store/db/postgres/memo.go`** (line 89), **`store/db/mysql/memo.go`** (line 104). `find.VisibilityList` becomes a `` `memo`.`visibility` IN (...) `` WHERE clause. This is the mechanism the RSS/frontend/stats/ListMemos filters rely on.

## Attachment / resource serving — three separate surfaces

**`server/router/fileserver/fileserver.go`** — `checkAttachmentPermission` (lines 650-704). The raw file-serving path, independent of gRPC:
```go
if memo.Visibility == store.Public && s.Profile.AllowAnonymous() { return nil }
// share_token fallback for private/protected...
if memo.Visibility == store.Private && user.ID != memo.CreatorID && user.Role != store.RoleAdmin {
    return Forbidden
}
```
Note: unlinked attachments (MemoID == nil) are creator/admin-only (lines 651-664), and it also honors a `share_token` query param (lines 684-689).

**`server/router/api/v1/attachment_service.go`** — `checkAttachmentAccess` (lines 419-455), called from `GetAttachmentBinary` at line 256:
```go
if memo.Visibility == store.Public { return nil }
if user == nil { return Unauthenticated }
if memo.Visibility == store.Private && memo.CreatorID != user.ID && !isSuperUser(user) {
    return PermissionDenied
}
```

**`server/router/api/v1/memo_attachment_service.go`** — `ListMemoAttachments` (lines 213-225). Inline duplicate of the same rule guarding the list of a memo's attachments.

## SSE (server-sent events) — delivery filtering by visibility

**`server/router/api/v1/sse_hub.go`** — `SSEClient.canReceive` (lines 134-144). Events are filtered before delivery to each subscribed client:
```go
switch event.Visibility {
case store.Private:
    return c.userID == event.CreatorID || c.role == store.RoleAdmin
case store.Public, store.Protected, "":
    return true
default:
    return false // unknown visibility -> deny
}
```
The `Visibility`/`CreatorID` on the event are populated at broadcast sites (e.g. `memo_service.go:166-167` via `resolveSSECreatorID`). Note: PROTECTED events are delivered to all connected clients here.

## RSS feed

**`server/router/rss/rss.go`** — `GetExploreRSS` (line 90) and `GetUserRSS` (line 141). Both hardcode `VisibilityList: []store.Visibility{store.Public}`.

## Frontend (SSR / sitemap)

**`server/router/frontend/frontend.go`** — `getSitemapXML` (lines 149-151): `VisibilityList: []store.Visibility{store.Public}`. This is the only visibility gate in the frontend service; there is no per-memo SSR meta-tag handler that applies its own check (the frontend otherwise serves the SPA).

## Reactions

**`server/router/api/v1/reaction_service.go`** — `UpsertMemoReaction`/related (lines 30-38) and a second site at line 83:
```go
if memo.Visibility != store.Public { ... }
if memo.Visibility == store.Private && memo.CreatorID != user.ID && !isSuperUser(user) {
    return PermissionDenied
}
```

## Comments

**`server/router/api/v1/memo_service_comments.go`** — `CreateMemoComment` (line 41) gates comment creation by the parent memo's visibility; `ListMemoComments` (line 148) delegates to `checkMemoReadAccess`.

## Related (not viewer-access gates, but visibility-conditioned delivery — noting for completeness)

- **`server/router/api/v1/user_service_stats.go`** (lines 84-90, 218-220) — builds `VisibilityList` (Public, or Public+Protected for the owner) when computing another user's stats.
- **`server/router/api/v1/memo_mention_helpers.go`** (lines 62, 67, 84) — suppresses mention notifications for private memos the target can't see.
- **`server/router/api/v1/user_service_notifications.go`** (lines 309-312) and **`server/notification/email.go`** (lines 313-316) — redact/label notification content by visibility; these are outbound-notification filters, not request-time view gates.

### Summary of distinct enforcement surfaces
1. gRPC/Connect API single-memo gate — `checkMemoReadAccess` (memo_service.go)
2. gRPC/Connect API list gate — `ListMemos` filter construction (memo_service.go) → store SQL (`store/db/*/memo.go`)
3. Fileserver attachment serving — `checkAttachmentPermission` (fileserver.go)
4. API attachment serving — `checkAttachmentAccess` + `ListMemoAttachments`
5. SSE delivery filter — `canReceive` (sse_hub.go)
6. RSS — `GetExploreRSS`/`GetUserRSS`
